course: dictionary
lesson: 9290
title: Spartan: a people, a plain life
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word with a capital letter often names a place or a people. Capital «Spartan» comes from Sparta, a city in ancient Greece. «In Sparta boys left home at seven to train hard as soldiers.» So a Spartan is a person from Sparta, and the Spartans were famous for being tough.
explain: With a small letter, spartan is an adjective: it describes things. A «spartan room» has almost nothing in it, with no comfort and no decoration. A «spartan lifestyle» is simple and strict, with no luxuries. The words near spartan tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If a room has one bed, one chair and bare walls, you can say it is spartan. If a sentence says «the Spartans held the pass», spartan is a person, so start with a capital letter.
fact: A Spartan was a person from Sparta, a city in ancient Greece.
fact: «In Sparta boys left home at seven to train hard as soldiers.»
fact: «Spartan» with a small letter means very simple and plain, without comfort or decoration.
fact: «Spartan» can also mean strict, tough and self-disciplined, as in «a spartan lifestyle».
fact: In 480 BC, King Leonidas and 300 Spartans held the narrow pass of Thermopylae for three days against a huge Persian army.
exercise: «In Sparta boys left home at seven to train hard as soldiers.» Who were Spartans? | *People from Sparta, a city in ancient Greece | Kings of Persia | Sailors from Athens | Teachers in modern London
exercise: Maya's bedroom is spartan: one bed, one chair and bare walls. What does spartan mean here? | *Very plain, with no comfort or decoration | Very noisy and crowded | Covered in paintings from floor to ceiling | Full of toys and bright colours
exercise: Coach Reid says his team must be spartan in training: no sweets, early nights and hard practice. What does spartan suggest? | Silly and loud | Wet and muddy | *Strict, tough and self-disciplined
test: Which sentence uses spartan as a person, not as a describing word? | A spartan lifestyle is strict | *The Spartans held the pass at Thermopylae | Her spartan breakfast was one biscuit | The room looked spartan
test: What is a spartan lifestyle like? | Quiet and lazy | Rich, with lots of feasts | Noisy and cheerful | *Simple and tough, with no luxuries
exam: Which words best describe a «spartan room»? | *Plain, simple and almost empty | Bright, crowded and full of toys | Grand, golden and full of mirrors | Wet, grey and dreich
